ng the trees, hard by, having their branches tossed by the wind.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.931,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-1-70"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4001040","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c98e5d698e0e1afd13bdf5f82ba1e5f85eed8ba44080f0080c55fd6e31828d72","compact":"642cda9589f81cd088dc54302a017be9a1de25886becae56d8b669360de92fb4","nasal":"5048ecd0f135d0addd98666640ff0dd12c55c48825a3e4586f7d7be7fb4e340d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-1-41","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":1,"verse":41,"english":"O Saumitri, the mountainous levels variegated with flowers of different species, are appearing like to beds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-1-74"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4001041","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"072f56b04ed3d4dd125c2cd23648c375212777955ba3b17e202bda0c2698e295","compact":"994df45f233e9194d1abc7923de79b9a8906135294b917907e031c2b88228956","nasal":"994df45f233e9194d1abc7923de79b9a8906135294b917907e031c2b88228956"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-1-42","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":1,"verse":42,"english":"Behold O Saumitri, the origination of flowers in the trees at the expiry of the winter. The trees as if viewing with each other, have blossomed in this season of flowers. The trees, O Lakşmaņa, with bees humming around and with flowery branches are as if welcoming each other.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-1-75"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4001042","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"683a9b7e85e73b8816e6363153e35b679a4f82568d33c5d42012162e9273bf83","compact":"5381d0962fcb2c0a2c2e1f99c135af3e5645f62ad7c5fea83b57f4853